WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.100 --> 00:00:01.760
Which way should a polynomial

2
00:00:01.760 --> 00:00:04.340
reduction point? A reduction from

3
00:00:04.340 --> 00:00:06.100
A to B transforms each

4
00:00:06.100 --> 00:00:08.020
A instance into one B

5
00:00:08.020 --> 00:00:09.980
instance with the same yes-or-no

6
00:00:09.980 --> 00:00:12.120
answer. A solver for B

7
00:00:12.120 --> 00:00:14.020
then solves A, so A

8
00:00:14.020 --> 00:00:15.400
is no harder than B,

9
00:00:15.640 --> 00:00:16.680
not the other way around.

10
00:00:17.180 --> 00:00:19.060
A complete proof must define

11
00:00:19.060 --> 00:00:21.640
the transformation, show valid output,

12
00:00:22.100 --> 00:00:23.840
prove both implications and bound

13
00:00:23.840 --> 00:00:25.620
construction time in the encoded

14
00:00:25.620 --> 00:00:28.120
input length. Polynomial output size

15
00:00:28.120 --> 00:00:29.740
follows from actually writing it

16
00:00:29.740 --> 00:00:32.240
in polynomial time. A reduction

17
00:00:32.240 --> 00:00:34.260
cannot simply say output yes

18
00:00:34.260 --> 00:00:35.480
if the input is a

19
00:00:35.480 --> 00:00:37.060
yes instance when deciding that

20
00:00:37.060 --> 00:00:38.940
condition is the original hard

21
00:00:38.940 --> 00:00:39.440
problem.

22
00:00:40.100 --> 00:00:41.760
For Independent Set to Clique,

23
00:00:42.360 --> 00:00:43.580
keep the vertex set and

24
00:00:43.580 --> 00:00:45.520
threshold but complement the graph’s

25
00:00:45.520 --> 00:00:48.160
edges between distinct vertices. Two

26
00:00:48.160 --> 00:00:50.420
selected vertices are nonadjacent in

27
00:00:50.420 --> 00:00:52.300
the original graph exactly when

28
00:00:52.300 --> 00:00:53.320
they are adjacent in the

29
00:00:53.320 --> 00:00:55.840
complement. Do not add self-loops;

30
00:00:56.380 --> 00:00:58.200
only unordered distinct pairs are

31
00:00:58.200 --> 00:00:58.640
toggled.

32
00:00:59.100 --> 00:01:00.420
If the original graph has

33
00:01:00.420 --> 00:01:01.680
an independent set of size

34
00:01:01.680 --> 00:01:03.420
at least k, all its

35
00:01:03.420 --> 00:01:05.440
selected distinct pairs become complement

36
00:01:05.440 --> 00:01:06.840
edges, so it is a

37
00:01:06.840 --> 00:01:09.780
clique. Conversely, a complement clique

38
00:01:09.780 --> 00:01:11.560
has no original edges among

39
00:01:11.560 --> 00:01:13.520
its selected vertices, so it

40
00:01:13.520 --> 00:01:15.660
is independent. Testing every vertex

41
00:01:15.660 --> 00:01:17.580
pair constructs the complement in

42
00:01:17.580 --> 00:01:18.600
polynomial time.

43
00:01:18.980 --> 00:01:20.360
If Clique were in P,

44
00:01:20.700 --> 00:01:22.680
this mapping would place Independent

45
00:01:22.680 --> 00:01:24.860
Set in P. The reduction

46
00:01:24.860 --> 00:01:26.380
alone does not prove that

47
00:01:26.380 --> 00:01:28.280
either problem is already in

48
00:01:28.280 --> 00:01:29.920
P or that either lies

49
00:01:29.920 --> 00:01:32.380
outside P. Hardness arguments require

50
00:01:32.380 --> 00:01:33.660
